From 6be9923cc72f3e49f8af5f1447e26e802f7d9f38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yago Lasse <yagolasse@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:09:26 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] linux: x86-64 trapped MMIO (APU, AC'97, OHCI) through a
 ucontext bridge

On POSIX only arm64 had a trapped-MMIO decoder, so on Linux x86-64
xbox_PosixMmioFault returned 0: OHCI switched itself off (no pads), the
AC'97 bus-master write trap was not armed, and the first trapped APU
register access was a crash.

mmio_decode.h now builds on Linux x86-64 too: the decoder works on
mmio_ctx_t (CONTEXT on Win32, a CONTEXT-shaped struct on Linux), and
mmio_emulate_ucontext copies a signal handler's gregs[] in and back
(kernel sigcontext order; only CF/ZF/SF/OF are written back to EFLAGS).
The APU hook, the AC'97 POSIX trap, OHCI and xbox_PosixMmioFault use it
there as they use the A64 decoder on arm64. Win32 is unchanged.

Tests: mmio_decode builds on Linux x86-64 and adds a gregs round-trip
case (slot order, rip, flags kept); usb_ohci_posix runs on x86-64 Linux
instead of skipping.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MpLs2w6Qd9WdNHUWmKSXXn
